Q: Mongodb update array within an array of docs, using ID A: <blockquote>
<h2>Adding a resident</h2>
</blockquote>
<pre><code>db.Suburbs.findOneAndUpdate(
    { &quot;_id&quot;: ObjectId(&quot;000000000000000000001001&quot;) },
    {
        $push: { &quot;Houses.$[myIdentifier].Residents&quot;: &quot;NewPerson&quot; }
    },
    {
        arrayFilters: [{ &quot;myIdentifier._id&quot;: ObjectId(&quot;000000000000000000002002&quot;) }]
    }
);

If you want to add multiple residents at once, you can combine $push with $each:

$push: { &quot;Houses.$[myIdentifier].Residents&quot;: { $each: [&quot;Alice&quot;, &quot;Bob&quot;] } }
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Removing a resident:</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<pre><code>db.Suburbs.findOneAndUpdate(
    { &quot;_id&quot;: ObjectId(&quot;000000000000000000001001&quot;) },
    {
        $pull: { &quot;Houses.$[myIdentifier].Residents&quot;: &quot;Johnny&quot; }
    },
    {
        arrayFilters: [{ &quot;myIdentifier._id&quot;: ObjectId(&quot;000000000000000000002002&quot;) }]
    }
);
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p>Only use $set when you want to update <strong>NumFloors.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
